Under 'How they got there', state the result, then describe the team's profile using the first three stats in that list.
Under 'Would the model have picked them?', compare the model's probability with the base rate and the rank, and name the stage given as nearest to the model's expectation. Exactly two teams reach each final, so the model picked a team only if it ranked in its top two; ranks three and four make it a leading contender; any lower rank means it did not pick them, even when the probability beat the base rate. The model never saw this season but was trained on the other seasons, including later ones, so describe whether it would have picked them, not a forecast made at the time.
Under 'Weak spots', name the last two or three stats in that list; if the team beat more than half of teams on every stat, say it had no clear weak spot. You may add one sentence on a stat from 'Stats that pushed the prediction down most' on which the team beat most teams, saying the model marked it down although the team ranked well on it.

